{
  "slug": "preterito",
  "number": 11,
  "part": 3,
  "level": "A2",
  "title": "The preterite",
  "tagline": "Hablé, comí, fui: finished actions in the past.",
  "goal": "Form the preterite of regular verbs, handle the spelling changes, and memorize the most common irregular preterites (fui, tuve, hice, dije…).",
  "minutes": 12,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "regulares",
      "title": "Regular verbs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The preterite (*pretérito*) tells **completed actions** at a specific moment: *Ayer hablé con ella* (Yesterday I spoke with her)."
        },
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": ["yo", "tú", "él / ella / usted", "nosotros", "ellos / ellas / ustedes"],
          "verbs": [
            { "verb": "hablar", "meaning": "to speak", "forms": ["habl{é}", "habl{aste}", "habl{ó}", "habl{amos}", "habl{aron}"] },
            { "verb": "comer", "meaning": "to eat", "forms": ["com{í}", "com{iste}", "com{ió}", "com{imos}", "com{ieron}"] },
            { "verb": "vivir", "meaning": "to live", "forms": ["viv{í}", "viv{iste}", "viv{ió}", "viv{imos}", "viv{ieron}"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "The accent matters",
          "text": "*hablo* (I speak) / *habló* (he spoke). *Hablamos* is both «we speak» and «we spoke»: context decides."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ortografia",
      "title": "Spelling changes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To keep the same sound, some **yo** forms change their spelling:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Ending", "yo", "Examples"],
          "rows": [
            ["*-car*", "c → qu", "*buscar → bus{qu}é, tocar → to{qu}é*"],
            ["*-gar*", "g → gu", "*llegar → lle{gu}é, pagar → pa{gu}é*"],
            ["*-zar*", "z → c", "*empezar → empe{c}é, almorzar → almor{c}é*"],
            ["vowel + *-er / -ir*", "i → y (he, they)", "*leer → le{y}ó, le{y}eron; oír → o{y}ó*"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "irregulares",
      "title": "Irregular preterites",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": ["yo", "tú", "él / ella / usted", "nosotros", "ellos / ellas / ustedes"],
          "verbs": [
            { "verb": "ser / ir", "meaning": "to be / to go", "forms": ["{fui}", "{fuiste}", "{fue}", "{fuimos}", "{fueron}"] },
            { "verb": "tener", "meaning": "to have", "forms": ["{tuv}e", "{tuv}iste", "{tuv}o", "{tuv}imos", "{tuv}ieron"] },
            { "verb": "hacer", "meaning": "to do", "forms": ["{hic}e", "{hic}iste", "{hiz}o", "{hic}imos", "{hic}ieron"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Verb", "Stem", "yo / él"],
          "rows": [
            ["*estar*", "estuv-", "*estuve, estuvo*"],
            ["*poder*", "pud-", "*pude, pudo*"],
            ["*poner*", "pus-", "*puse, puso*"],
            ["*querer*", "quis-", "*quise, quiso*"],
            ["*saber*", "sup-", "*supe, supo*"],
            ["*venir*", "vin-", "*vine, vino*"],
            ["*decir*", "dij-", "*dije, dijo, dijeron*"],
            ["*traer*", "traj-", "*traje, trajo, trajeron*"],
            ["*dar*", "—", "*di, dio* (like -er verbs)"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "text": "Irregular preterites have **no accent**: *tuve, hizo, vino*. And -ir stem changers change in he / they: *pedir → pidió, pidieron; dormir → durmió, durmieron*."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "regulares",
      "section": "regulares",
      "title": "Regular preterite",
      "instructions": "Write the verb in the preterite.",
      "kind": "type",
      "items": [
        { "prompt": "Ayer ___ con mi mamá. (hablar, yo)", "answer": "hablé" },
